            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 9 changed paths. The new review bind and record verbs are thin wiring in engine/cmd/review.go over review/app, gitexec and fsstore, whose source is outside this candidate and so is not evidence here.",
              "Input handling in engine/cmd/review.go is strict: parseReviewFlags rejects unknown flags, missing values, duplicate flags and positional arguments; --base, --head and --feature are required.",
              "Reply reading is bounded: readReviewReply wraps the reader in io.LimitReader at review.MaxReplyBytes+1, and git output is capped at reviewGitMaxOutput with a 5-minute timeout.",
              "Tests in engine/cmd/review_test.go cover the main exploit paths: option-like revisions (--output=...), path-traversal and unsafe feature names, symlinks at odd, odd/review-results and the feature directory, tampered digest echoes, and oversized replies. They assert that nothing is written outside odd/review-results and that exit code 2 is returned for refused replies.",
              "The shell forwarder in bin/lib/engine_verbs.sh uses exec with quoted \"$@\", so there is no shell injection. The new dispatch case in bin/labdrian-overlay is additive and does not change existing verbs.",
              "No secrets or dependency changes are introduced, and no reachable exploit caused by this candidate is demonstrated, so there are no findings."
            ]
          }
        }
