                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Read all nine changed paths in full. The review verbs are cleanly structured: parseReviewFlags, require, reviewPath and the two run functions are small and commented, and the exit-code contract (0, 1, 2) is documented consistently across the shell usage, Go usage and tests.",
              "The only maintainability concern found is the duplicated 150000 literal in the usage text and the test, which can drift from review.DiffLimitBytes. It is low impact and not a defect of behavior."
