            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R3-001",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/cmd/review.go:262",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "writeReviewJSON ignores the error from p.stdout.Write and then exits 0. If stdout is closed or broken (for example a closed pipe), 'review bind' or 'review record' reports success, although the caller never received the binding or the handoff skeleton. For 'record', the result file has already been stored at that point. The failure needs an unusual stdout state, so it is a warning.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/cmd/review.go:262-263"
                ],
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Read all 9 changed paths in full. The Go flag parsing rejects unknown flags, missing values, repeated flags and positional arguments. The tests cover each of these rejections, and they also assert that no worktree directory is created for a refused command line.",
              "The exit-code contract is observable and tested: 0 on success, 2 for a refused reply (with nothing written), 1 for any other failure. The tests cover unsafe feature names, symlinks on the results path, an unreadable --result file, an unresolvable commit, and a directory outside any repository. The built-binary test exercises bind, record, the numbering of repeated records, a tampered reply, and `roles validate` on the printed skeleton.",
              "The reply read is capped at MaxReplyBytes+1 bytes, so an oversized reply is refused without being read in full. This is covered by a test.",
              "The git adapter is built with a timeout and an output cap. A unit test asserts the environment and the deadline that reach it.",
              "The shell forwarding, the dispatch route, the usage text and the shell dispatch-table row are consistent with each other and tested at the cheapest level.",
              "The only gap I found is the ignored stdout write error, reported as the warning above."
            ]
          }
        }
